        <mxCell id="notes" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffcc;strokeColor=#d6b656;spacing=6;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes / assumptions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• J6 pin map from docs/Custom boards/tinyControlBoard/TinyControlboard.md §3; UART/handshake GPIOs from docs/DeveloperGuides/06-hardware-interface.md §3.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Conflict:&lt;/b&gt; the KiCad doc names GPIO9-14, 39, 47 as above, but firmware (06-hardware-interface.md §6) uses GPIO13 = 3.3 V rail, GPIO12 = DAC power, GPIO9 = output stage, GPIO11 = Pi power, GPIO10 = DAC signal-select, GPIO47/39 = general relays 1/2. Which J6 line carries which firmware function must be confirmed against the schematic.&lt;br&gt;• Likewise GPIO1/2 (firmware UART2 RX/TX) are listed as spare in the KiCad doc; GPIO41 is called esp_ir_sent on the board and ESP→Pi data-ready in firmware.&lt;br&gt;• Debug TX/RX are assumed to be UART0 (TXD0/RXD0 on the module); the doc does not give the exact mapping to J6 pins 5/6.&lt;br&gt;• Outputs are logic-level 5 V from a TXS0108E (documented as a poor fit for driving relays/mains directly); external driver stages and isolation are not on this board.&lt;br&gt;• J6 is identical to J3 (Molex 70246-4001) – do not cross the ribbon cables." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="950" x="20" y="1060" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
